Perform client services and support the State Compliance department on day-to-day duties:
Review questionnaire and business model assessment with client;
Consolidate & compile applications;
Review applications for accuracy and completion;
Review outgoing and incoming physical mail (electronically if working remote);
Manage client communication and ensure their needs are met;
Assist Application Specialist in resolving deficiencies highlighted by the Board on behalf of clients;
Update internal database to reflect application progression;
Administrative work (basic Microsoft Word skills required);
Special projects may be assigned on an as-needed basis.
